recommendations.decision:
Contract v1. Each adapter must supply:
- engine, engine_version, adapter_version and contract_version;
- the IR hash and the analysis-sample row indices;
- a coefficient map from engine names to canonical IR columns, with aliased flags;
- the criterion (REML, ML, Laplace, AGQ(k), nAGQ0, VB, MAP) and whether the reported likelihood is exact;
- the weights semantics (precision, frequency or log-likelihood multiplier);
- beta;
- the absolute covariance matrix for each IR block, in canonical term order, with its packing order declared;
- sigma2 or the dispersion, in the registry's canonical parameterisation;
- the reported objective with its constant convention;
- vcov(beta) with a method label (conditional on theta, joint observed Hessian, finite-difference Hessian, expected information or posterior);
- the raw convergence output (flag, optimiser, iterations, messages tagged by source).
Optional capability flags: X and Z (for verification only), labelled BLUPs and conditional variances (for cross-checking only), objective_fn, refit(start, criterion, rows), simulate and df. A missing capability yields 'not_available'. On every fit the suite then (1) runs an objective-match test: |reported - reference at the reported estimates| <= max(1e-6*|dev|, 1e-6), otherwise status contract_mismatch and Stream A stops; (2) measures the gap to the best known objective, using a multi-start or boundary probe for small q, plus a reference gradient and Hessian, with statuses at_optimum, near or not_converged whatever the engine's flag says; (3) recomputes BLUPs, conditional variances (beta fixed, with PEV including beta uncertainty labelled separately), residuals, P-based quantities, a scale-free singularity verdict and vcov(beta) under one declared convention.
